WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:19.470
Clark lowered the car window and gazed at the brand-new bike track.

2
00:00:22.292 --> 00:00:25.714
It twisted through a huge green field like a brown snake.

3
00:00:26.654 --> 00:00:29.496
Dirt had been piled up here and there to form jumps.

4
00:00:30.192 --> 00:00:33.154
A big mud pit looked like trouble for riders.

5
00:00:34.214 --> 00:00:40.538
Riley's heartbeat sped up when she spotted the Blue Demons team banner—and the large crowd.

6
00:00:40.558 --> 00:00:44.380
"Nervous, Riley?"

7
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.781
her father asked.

8
00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.122
"Who, me?"

9
00:00:47.842 --> 00:00:48.603
Riley joked.

10
00:00:48.623 --> 00:00:51.184
"Nerves-of-Steel Riley?"

11
00:00:52.105 --> 00:00:53.005
Then she paused.

12
00:00:53.025 --> 00:00:55.707
"A little," she admitted.

13
00:00:55.727 --> 00:00:57.848
"I really want to make the team."

14
00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:02.449
The Blue Demons were the best mountain bike team in the state.

15
00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:08.210
Today's event was an open practice, which meant anyone could ride and test the track.

16
00:01:09.371 --> 00:01:12.832
The Blue Demons were holding the real team tryout next Saturday.

17
00:01:12.852 --> 00:01:15.092
"You'll do great!"

18
00:01:16.073 --> 00:01:21.494
Riley's older sister, Jordan, grabbed the headrest and pulled herself forward from the backseat.

19
00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:25.015
"Don't let all these people rattle you."

20
00:01:25.035 --> 00:01:28.256
"I'm not scared," Riley replied.

21
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.081
"I eat fear for breakfast!"

22
00:01:32.761 --> 00:01:33.601
Jordan laughed.

23
00:01:34.221 --> 00:01:36.002
"That's my line.

24
00:01:36.822 --> 00:01:38.503
But I'll let you borrow it today.

25
00:01:39.743 --> 00:01:43.524
And don't forget—where your brain goes, your body will follow."

26
00:01:44.584 --> 00:01:47.765
Jordan was 17, five years older than Riley.

27
00:01:48.665 --> 00:01:51.926
Riley had started mountain biking because Jordan was a rider.

28
00:01:53.066 --> 00:01:56.667
But Riley had quickly discovered her own fierce love of the sport.

29
00:01:58.108 --> 00:02:04.851
Unfortunately, Jordan hadn't been on a bike for months—not since a terrible bike accident last fall.

30
00:02:05.832 --> 00:02:11.395
She was still recovering from the crash; she wore a brace on one leg and used crutches to

31
00:02:11.455 --> 00:02:13.756
walk. Mr.

32
00:02:13.796 --> 00:02:18.799
Clark walked around to the rack on the back of the car and helped Riley remove her battered

33
00:02:18.899 --> 00:02:20.560
but beloved Supertrek.

34
00:02:25.682 --> 00:02:28.604
It had been Jordan's first bike, her lucky bike.

35
00:02:29.884 --> 00:02:34.746
Riley parked her bike, and then she and her father got into line at a tent to register.

36
00:02:39.828 --> 00:02:40.669
us to stay with you?"

37
00:02:41.189 --> 00:02:42.189
Mr. Clark asked.

38
00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:44.210
"I'll be fine, Dad.

39
00:02:44.511 --> 00:02:45.511
It's only practice."

40
00:02:46.611 --> 00:02:50.453
"Okay. We'll all be here for the tryout next weekend, rooting for you."

41
00:02:54.455 --> 00:03:02.228
Mr. Clark signed some registration forms, and Riley pulled out her new prized possession: an official USA Cycling

42
00:03:02.288 --> 00:03:07.771
license. Coach Adams, the Blue Demons head coach, spotted it.

43
00:03:07.791 --> 00:03:12.154
"Congratulations on becoming a member of USA Cycling, Riley!"

44
00:03:12.174 --> 00:03:14.076
"Thanks, Coach."

45
00:03:14.096 --> 00:03:19.159
"You'll need that license next week at the tryout," he added.

46
00:03:19.179 --> 00:03:24.603
"Today the junior division riders will ride the practice trail from ten to eleven o'clock."

47
00:03:24.623 --> 00:03:27.325
"Cool," Riley said.

48
00:03:27.345 --> 00:03:31.207
A few minutes later, she walked her father back to the car.

49
00:03:34.809 --> 00:03:37.530
be back at eleven," he said, looking worried.

50
00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.092
"I'll be careful, I promise."

51
00:03:41.172 --> 00:03:43.093
He gave her a quick kiss on the forehead.

52
00:03:43.113 --> 00:03:45.615
"Love you, peanut.

53
00:03:46.255 --> 00:03:48.637
Now go and eat them for breakfast!"

54
00:03:49.837 --> 00:03:53.239
"It's fear, Dad," Riley said patiently.

55
00:03:53.259 --> 00:03:57.242
"I eat fear for breakfast, not other riders.

56
00:03:57.602 --> 00:03:58.783
I'm not a zombie."

57
00:03:58.803 --> 00:04:01.265
"But you sure look like one!"

58
00:04:01.765 --> 00:04:03.146
Jordan yelled from the car.

59
00:04:03.166 --> 00:04:07.749
"Brains!" Riley clawed at the car window.

60
00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.451
"I need brains!"

61
00:04:10.471 --> 00:04:14.454
"Nice zombie impression," Jordan said.

62
00:04:14.474 --> 00:04:16.556
"Just don't ride like one!"

63
00:04:22.948 --> 00:04:25.970
After Jordan and Dad left, Riley checked her phone.

64
00:04:27.531 --> 00:04:28.511
It was nine thirty.

65
00:04:28.931 --> 00:04:31.093
She had thirty minutes to study the track.

66
00:04:32.273 --> 00:04:35.575
Mountain bike races were not races against individual riders.

67
00:04:36.736 --> 00:04:41.138
Each rider raced against the clock, and the rider with the fastest time won.

68
00:04:42.159 --> 00:04:44.940
So knowing the track in advance definitely paid off.

69
00:04:46.101 --> 00:04:51.124
Riley walked along the dirt trail, memorizing the location of soft spots and mud pits.

70
00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:58.582
She tried to gauge which turns and jumps she could take at full speed, and which ones would

71
00:04:58.622 --> 00:04:59.842
require more control.

72
00:05:00.943 --> 00:05:06.225
She also had to calculate how fast she could take the straightaways before going airborne for a jump.

73
00:05:08.206 --> 00:05:11.307
Looking at the jumps suddenly made Riley feel nervous again.

74
00:05:12.247 --> 00:05:14.248
Jordan had crashed while making a jump.

75
00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:18.630
She'd been in the lead at the Racing Raptors track on Hawk Mountain.

76
00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:23.592
Then Jordan went airborne for the jump and flew off her bike.

77
00:05:24.584 --> 00:05:31.387
She'd landed hard, and there was blood and an ambulance and— "Hey, watch where you're going!"

78
00:05:31.967 --> 00:05:33.388
A girl glared at Riley.

79
00:05:33.808 --> 00:05:35.068
"You almost knocked me over."

80
00:05:35.089 --> 00:05:37.910
"Sorry!" Riley said.

81
00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.590
"I didn't see you there."

82
00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:43.212
"Really? I'm not invisible," the girl snapped.

83
00:05:44.272 --> 00:05:45.953
She looked about the same age as Riley.

84
00:05:46.573 --> 00:05:50.755
She was tall, with leg muscles that showed she was an experienced rider.

85
00:05:50.775 --> 00:05:54.641
"Sorry," Riley apologized again.

86
00:05:55.381 --> 00:05:57.823
Then the girl's glittering bike caught her eye.

87
00:05:57.843 --> 00:06:02.305
"Wow! Is that the latest Fleet HD3?

88
00:06:02.325 --> 00:06:05.147
I didn't know it came with 24-inch wheels."

89
00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.348
"It doesn't."

90
00:06:08.048 --> 00:06:09.489
The girl strapped on her helmet.

91
00:06:09.509 --> 00:06:14.532
"My dad had this bike custom-built for me.

92
00:06:15.813 --> 00:06:17.474
For a huge amount of money, of course.

93
00:06:18.114 --> 00:06:21.416
I plan to make the team, and I need the best bike money can buy."

94
00:06:22.904 --> 00:06:26.747
Several replies raced through Riley's mind, none of them very nice.

95
00:06:27.828 --> 00:06:32.391
Luckily she heard her dad's voice inside her head: "Eat them for breakfast!"

96
00:06:33.511 --> 00:06:36.353
That made Riley smile instead of saying something nasty.

97
00:06:37.374 --> 00:06:42.918
Meanwhile the girl was staring at Riley's Supertrek, with its chipped paint and worn seat.

98
00:06:42.938 --> 00:06:45.399
"Your bike looks pretty old."

99
00:06:45.419 --> 00:06:49.282
"Yeah. It's a hand-me-down from my sister.

100
00:06:50.002 --> 00:06:52.024
My parents said I can get a new bike soon.

101
00:06:53.292 --> 00:06:55.793
But for now it's okay," Riley added.

102
00:06:55.813 --> 00:06:58.674
"I won a bunch of races on it last year.

103
00:06:59.774 --> 00:07:03.455
And I'm counting on it to get me the best time at the tryout next week too!"

104
00:07:04.535 --> 00:07:05.796
The girl's eyes narrowed.

105
00:07:05.816 --> 00:07:07.676
"We'll see about that!"

106
00:07:08.696 --> 00:07:11.097
She jumped on her bike and rode to the starting line.

107
00:07:16.218 --> 00:07:21.700
Riley followed as Delaney Thompson, the Blue Demons team captain, began making an announcement.

108
00:07:24.668 --> 00:07:28.690
As usual, his long dreadlocks hung in a cascade down his back.

109
00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.412
"Okay, everyone," he began.

110
00:07:32.432 --> 00:07:37.755
"This practice trail is a mile long, and we'll use it for the tryout trail next week too.

111
00:07:39.096 --> 00:07:43.278
Each of you can take as many practice runs today as you want during your division's hour.

112
00:07:44.539 --> 00:07:48.941
Riders will push off every thirty seconds, so pay attention and stay in line.

113
00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:53.384
When you're finished with one run, go to the back of the line to wait for another."

114
00:07:54.596 --> 00:07:59.340
All the junior riders jostled to get a place in line, and Riley noticed the girl with the

115
00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.882
expensive bike had managed to be first.

116
00:08:04.524 --> 00:08:09.168
Delaney blew his whistle and pressed his stopwatch, and the girl flew down the track.

117
00:08:12.871 --> 00:08:16.694
Riley watched as she hit each jump and took the curves like a pro.

118
00:08:24.832 --> 00:08:26.033
Who is that girl?"

119
00:08:27.074 --> 00:08:29.035
Delaney scanned the list on his clipboard.

120
00:08:29.055 --> 00:08:31.938
"New kid named Quinn Evans.

121
00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:34.860
She just moved here from Colorado."

122
00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:36.041
He looked up.

123
00:08:36.061 --> 00:08:40.764
"Fast turns aren't everything, Riley," he added softly.

124
00:08:40.784 --> 00:08:46.288
"Oh, and I have some bad news for girls trying out for the junior division.

125
00:08:47.409 --> 00:08:49.991
There are just two open spots on the team."
